+// RE4_DSP_BEHIND=1 (stage 3.4b): AX does not wait for the DSP. On the game's thread a list only moves its voices as
+// the DSP leaves them for AX to read back (AXVPB.c __AXServiceVPB: the state, the current address, the volume
+// envelope; the source's fraction decides how far the address goes): advance(). It goes into a queue with copies of
+// what AX changes later: the list, the chain's voices with their updates, the frame's sync flags and depops (patch
+// 0166), the CPU's aux position, the mode. The worker (or the game's thread at once, without one) mixes them in
+// order: its own copy of what depends on the samples (the ADPCM history, the source's last samples, the low-pass's,
+// the ramped mix volumes, the depop values) takes the CPU's values only where __AXServiceVPB wrote them (the sync
+// flags); it adds the depops up and fades them (AXSPB.c) itself, runs the aux callbacks on the CPU's buffer of the
+// frame (__AXProcessAux then skips them), keeps the last surround, and hands each block to the AI's ring
